From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 55/57] hjviewer: ui: desktop-chrome: pill tabs, window
 buttons, menus, install page and CM

The window chrome and the shared desktop menus in the new look (common/hjv_style.dart):

- Title bar: the tabs are soft 22 px pills, the selected one on the content colour with a thin
  border, the others quiet until hovered; the close button sits inside the pill (always on the
  selected tab). The window buttons are as tall as the bar and 40 px wide, the close button in
  danger; the bar's icon buttons (menu, add, tab list) have a rounded hover. The home and
  settings tabs use rounded icons (a gear for the settings).
- Menus (material_mod_popup_menu.dart, popup_menu.dart): 32 px rows (40 on a phone) inset from
  the menu's edges with a rounded hover in the palette's hover colour, icons in the secondary
  text colour, dividers with room around them, the theme's softer shadow, and 4 px of distance
  from the window's edges.
- button.dart: accent and outline buttons with radius 10 and palette hovers.
- Install page: the title with the app icon, the path and the shortcuts on one card, the licence
  as a quiet note, 40 px buttons with the main one last.
- Connection manager: the peer on a tinted card with a soft avatar tile, the permissions on a
  card with palette tiles, 36 px buttons with a visible hover, the title bar's close button like
  the main window's.
- The CM's tab list menu no longer renders as an error box: its Obx read no observable for a tab
  without a close callback.

Upstream's tab and install page builders stay, unused. No texts, keys or callbacks change.

After an independent review (screens in light and dark, the diff, the code rules):

- The palette's new tokens instead of the workarounds: the title bar's hovers (tabs, window
  buttons, the menu, add and tab list buttons) in hoverStrong; the close hovers (the window's,
  the CM's title bar) and the CM's red buttons in dangerFill.
- Accept and Elevate on the primary fill: white text on the success colour read below 3:1.
- The title bar's icon buttons take the pointer on their whole box again, as upstream's; the
  rounded hover is painted inside it.
- The CM's permission tiles: the icons of the off ones in the secondary text colour, at 20 px.
- The close confirmation's checkbox in line with the text above it.
- The CM's title bar close button: a _hjvBuild next to upstream's builder.
- The tab list menu's Obx condition back in upstream's order: making the CM's list show is a
  separate fix, not part of the new look.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
